  "corpus_id": "perseus-greek-known-author-v1",
  "description": "Original-language Ancient Greek prose: six cataloged authors, three distinct works each, plus a two-edition control of a separate Lucian work.",
  "selection_protocol": "Selected before scoring: choose three substantial, conventionally attributed distinct works per author, with at least 2,000 extracted Greek tokens each. Include three Attic forensic orators and two authors of Socratic prose for shared-genre/topic challenges. Lucian supplies a later author and a separate same-work edition control. No work, author, threshold, or feature is selected by observed benchmark accuracy.",
  "attribution_caveat": "Author identities are conventional Perseus catalog labels, not independent proof of ancient historical authorship. This is a small convenience benchmark of edited literary Greek, not scripture, and cannot validate biblical attribution, number of hands, or Hebrew/Arabic transfer. The same editor/edition tradition is often confounded with author; coarse genre/topic labels do not fully control subgenre, subject, chronology, or literary dependence. Forensic speeches may be ghostwritten for speakers; the author label refers to the attributed composer.",
  "known_disputed_works_excluded": [
    "Isocrates To Demonicus",
    "Plato Alcibiades II and other dubia/spuria",
    "Xenophon Constitution of the Athenians",
    "Lucian Macrobii and De astrologia"
  ],
  "date_downloaded": "2026-09-16",
  "repository_license_url": "https://github.com/PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit/blob/9839fe84c883e47ca5dab8872d8c684d9e14fe14/license.md",
  "parser_policy": "Extract only the single Greek edition within TEI body. Remove headers, notes, headings, speaker labels, bibliographic material, rejected readings/deletions, marked quotations/citations, and non-Greek spans. Keep main-text names and authored direct speech; select lem/corr/reg preferred readings. Normalize through the application Greek tokenizer; punctuation is omitted. Never count an alternate edition as an independent work.",
  "label_policy": "genre and topic are manually assigned broad challenge strata, not independent scholarly taxonomies. socratic_prose includes apology, dialogue, and recollection; forensic_oratory includes public and private cases.",
  "controls_note": "The two How to Write History files have the same work_id and role=witness_control. They are excluded from load_benchmark by default; they may be compared for edition sensitivity, never added as independent attribution works. Edition dates are reproduced as cataloged and have not been bibliographically corrected.",
